# Ignore everything in the user home directory by default
/*

# Except the project and the readme
!README.md
!.gitignore

# GitHub only reads workflows from .github/ at the REPOSITORY ROOT, which for
# this repo is the home directory -- so the CI config has to live here, above
# the project it builds. The /* rule above would swallow it: release.yml is
# tracked only because it was force-added once, and without this line any NEW
# file under .github/ (a second workflow, a composite action, dependabot.yml)
# is refused by `git add` and skipped silently by `git add -A`.
!.github/
!Documents/
Documents/*
!Documents/flac-downloader/
